  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "669Klqw5FA20dccNbozhw2P7G7Y=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T12:35:10.000Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "Adding to the toolbar is slot-addressed, not index-addressed. `customControls` is a `Partial<Record<ControlSlot, CustomToolbarControl | CustomToolbarControlList>>`, so each of `first`, `second` and `third` takes either a single control object or an array of them.\n\nA `CustomToolbarControl` is `{ component, position? }`, where `component` matches `ToolbarControlComponent` \u2014 a function taking `{ document?: PHDocument }` and returning `JSX.Element | null`. The toolbar passes the document it is operating on, which is the `document` prop when given and the currently selected document otherwise, so a custom control must treat `document` as optional.\n\n```tsx\n<DocumentToolbar\n  document={document}\n  customControls={{\n    second: {\n      position: \"end\",\n      component: ({ document }) => (\n        <button onClick={() => alert(document?.header.name)}>custom two</button>\n      ),\n    },\n  }}\n/>\n```\n\nTwo behaviours worth internalising:\n\n- **`position` defaults to `\"start\"`.** A custom control renders *before* the slot's built-in controls unless you set `position: \"end\"`. This surprises people who expect appended controls.\n- **Lists need a `key`.** When a slot receives a `CustomToolbarControlList`, each item is a `CustomToolbarControl & { key: React.Key }`. The key is passed straight to React; there is no implicit index fallback.\n\nThe mutual exclusivity with `children` is enforced by the type system, not by a runtime warning. `DocumentToolbarProps` is a union of `DocumentToolbarWithChildrenProps` (document, toolbarContainer, toolbarClassName, children) and `DocumentToolbarWithCustomControlsProps` (those three plus enabled/disabled controls, componentOverrides, customControls, controlsContainer, controlsContainerClassName). In `children` mode the toolbar renders only the children inside the toolbar container, so `customControls` and every other customization prop is unused \u2014 the slots themselves stop existing.\n\n_Source: apps/academy/docs/academy/03-Build/03-BuildingUserExperiences/06-DocumentTools/00-DocumentToolbar.mdx, confirmed against packages/design-system/src/connect/components/document-toolbar/types.ts (Powerhouse v6.2.2-dev.45)._",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-14T12:35:10.000Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T12:35:10.000Z"
    }
  },
